# Kapa

Monorepo for the Kapa platform. Every service is operated from the root `Makefile`.

## Requirements

- Docker with Compose v2 (`docker compose`)
- GNU Make

## Getting started

```bash
cp .env.example .env   # then set real production credentials
make run
```

## Commands

| Command       | Description                                                          |
|---------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `make run`    | Build and start services with production credentials (`.env`)        |
| `make stop`   | Stop and remove running containers (data is kept)                    |
| `make clean`  | Remove containers, volumes and built images — **destroys data**      |
| `make format` | Format code (N/A for now)                                            |
| `make lint`   | Lint code (N/A for now)                                              |
| `make test`   | Spin up an isolated stack with dev credentials, check health, clean  |
| `make help`   | List all targets                                                     |

## Environments

| File           | Purpose                       | Compose project | Host port | Committed |
|----------------|-------------------------------|-----------------|-----------|-----------|
| `.env`         | Production                    | `kapa`          | 5432      | No        |
| `.env.dev`     | Development / test            | `kapa-test`     | 55432     | Yes       |
| `.env.example` | Template for `.env`           | —               | —         | Yes       |

Production and test run as separate Compose projects, so `make test` never touches
production containers or data.

## Structure

```
kapa/
├── Makefile                  # single entry point for the whole repo
├── docker-compose.yml
├── .env.example / .env.dev
└── services/
    └── postgres/
        ├── Dockerfile        # postgres:<version>-alpine
        └── initdb/           # SQL/sh run once on first boot
```

